From 342d690da3dffd41bf70a68ef31b0a7210db8b48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wagzee <jurik17@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:39:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] glm-cuda: with bf16 dense weights, a prompt chunk takes 2,048
 rows

The recipe applies this patch to a PROMPT_CHUNK=2048 image (patches/engine/chunk2048/); PROMPT_CHUNK=auto picks it
for DENSE=bf16 on the pair, and every other image keeps 0094/0095's 4,096-row chunk. It sets prefill_rows and
DFlash2's MAX_CTX back to the 2,048 they were before 0094/0095, so it undoes exactly what they changed.

Why the width depends on the dense weights: a prompt pass has a fixed cost (cuda_exl3.zig: each call to the common
experts decodes every expert's weights, about 0.15 s a pass on the pair), which a wider chunk spreads over more rows.
With q8 dense the rest of a pass costs the same per row at any width, so 4,096 wins (+7% in 0094; 2,048 measured
4.4% slower on 2026-11-16). With bf16 dense, a pass costs 0.54 ms a row up to about 2,800 rows and 1.3 ms a row past
about 3,000, so a 4,096-row chunk spends more in its last rows than it saves in fixed cost. The step was not profiled; the bf16 dense
matmul path is the part that differs between the two settings.

Measured on the pair (main 80be4d6 at its defaults, a cold 34.7K prompt): bf16 1,321 -> 1,701 tok/s (+29%), its first
token beside a decoding chat 37.1 -> 29.7 s, the chat's worst pause 3.37 -> 1.46 s; q8 1,791 -> 1,712 tok/s (-4.4%),
pause 2.60 -> 1.46 s. The chat's rate during the prompt does not change (PREFILL_SHARE sets it).

Exact: as 0094 notes, a pair's sums do not depend on which chunk holds it, and greedy replies at 30, 2,987 and 8,859
prompt tokens hash the same at both widths, with q8 and with bf16. Kept prompt states are cut at the chunk's step, so
with LEARN_GIB a state written by one width is not resumed by the other: measured both ways, the turn prefills (or
resumes the image's own state) with the same reply and no error. The finer grid resumes more of a repeated prompt:
10,240 of 11,678 tokens against 8,192.
---
 zig/src/families/glm/cuda_state.zig | 2 +-
 zig/src/families/glm/dflash.zig     | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_state.zig b/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_state.zig
index 10d16cb..ddd8a2b 100644
--- a/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_state.zig
+++ b/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_state.zig
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@ const mlp = @import("cuda_mlp.zig");
 const kda_block = @import("cuda_kda_block.zig");
 
 /// A prompt chunk's rows (decode.PREFILL_ROWS).
-pub const prefill_rows = 4096;
+pub const prefill_rows = 2048;
 /// A decode window's rows (Engine's max_rows): the pending token and up to 31 drafts or copied tokens (upstream #2257's
 /// width; DFlash2 still drafts 7 a block, so the rows past 8 serve context copies).
 pub const window_rows = 32;
diff --git a/zig/src/families/glm/dflash.zig b/zig/src/families/glm/dflash.zig
index d4b97cc..b2aaa7a 100644
--- a/zig/src/families/glm/dflash.zig
+++ b/zig/src/families/glm/dflash.zig
@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@ pub const CH: usize = 16; // key chunks of the chunked attention (df_attn_part)
 pub const CW: usize = 2 * TOPK; // a row's gathered ints: 16 ids, then 16 values' bits
 pub const MAX_S: usize = 16; // streams one block pass drafts for
 pub const MAX_M: usize = MAX_S * BLOCK; // block rows at most
-pub const MAX_CTX: usize = 4096; // context rows one ingest takes (a prompt chunk's)
+pub const MAX_CTX: usize = 2048; // context rows one ingest takes (a prompt chunk's)
 pub const STEP_ROWS: usize = 32; // a verify's tap rows (the shared windows' rows at most)
 pub const TAP_ROW: usize = taps_mod.layers.len * D * 2; // bytes of one row's taps
 
